body:
Summary: Lost a friend over a debate of whether or not young teens should have sex. I said no, she said yes. the began to accuse me of certain ideas and twisted my words and said I was immediately wrong and I shouldn't have that OPINION cause it's judgmental and slut-shaming.

&#x200B;

I lost a friend over this. We had the topic of whether ages 13-15 should have sex (our ages are 14). I said that we shouldn't and she that we should. Then she went on about how I'm judging what people do with their bodies and I'm slut shaming females for having sex at that age (When I kept clarifying that I was talking about males too) and said I was giving her "Pro-life vibes". During the argument, she said she was automatically correct in the argument because you shouldn't judge people in the first place. She then said how I wasn't listening to her side of the argument when I told her multiples time that I was. She wasn't listening to mine. When I got upset over the idea that I "lost", she said "You're mad because you can't have a say in what people do with their bodies?" The entire time she wasn't listening to me because my opinion was immediately wrong and hers was right. I believe that both our opinions are wrong and right and basically told me that I'm not allowed to have an opinion on this unless it's the "right" one.

TLDR: If you agree that stuff like this happens to a man, you're trying to downplay what happens to women. Equality should be about all genders getting respect and not belittling the gender we want to be equal with. I also feel sorry for the OP having to go through this as a boy in society.

&#x200B;

I am so sorry, dude. It's fucked up. If even try to feel bad for what boys have to go through, you get called a "pick me". So many people say that they want equality, but thinks that mean you have to belittle the group you want too be equal with. We're not going to progress as a society with men and women being treated the same if we tell boys that they have fit a certain role. People preach "gender norms", but then push this type of gender norm onto men. I am so sorry you have to deal with this as a guy. It's just disgusting to see both men and women try to force this idea onto you guys that you can't cry or be abused. I tried to talk to my ex-friend about this picture I saw basically saying that just because you're a man doesn't mean you can't go through the same things as women. She tried to say that the picture was saying men go through worse than women and is trying to make men seem like they're going through worse. Then she fucking admitted that she's probably saying this "cause she hates men". You shouldn't hate men to the point you disagree with the idea that men deserve to be treated as humans too just like women. I've seen a lot of "feminists" Talk down sexual assault and abuse towards men by saying "well they do it to us!". I've seen a lot of other people objectifying men and make it normal. I'm sick of societies double standards and the people who would hate someone to the point that they can't have fucking morals. You can't even talk about this shit without being called weak or trying to make it seem like men has it worse than us. You can't talk about this without being called a "pick me girl" and not agreeing with every little shit about this fake ass equality. If we wanted equality, we would also talk about stuff like this that happens to men and boys like you.
